      "message": "\u003e If we can\u0027t handle the additional imports/updates\n\nAgree it would be bad if that\u0027s the case. Just to assure, the work I am doing here going to keep updating hickory-proto to the latest version (in fact I still depending on some changes in the upstreaming process). I am trying to take small step at a time by migrating the legacy v0.24.x versions first.\n\n\nThat said, I realize this v0.24.x, it\u0027s depending on an old version of \"thiserror\"\n```\nlujc@lujc-android-builder:~/android/master/external/rust/android-crates-io$ ./crate_tool analyze-updates hickory-proto\nAnalyzing updates to hickory-proto v0.24.1\nVersion 0.24.2\n  Dep idna ^1.0 is not satisfied by v0.5.0 at external/rust/android-crates-io/crates/idna\n  Dep thiserror ^1.0.20 is not satisfied by v2.0.11 at external/rust/android-crates-io/crates/thiserror\n    But the current version has the same dependency and it seems to work.\n```\n\nI will hold on this change for a while, to see if I can update and have the dependencies exact matching the vendored crates. \nOther crates imported in this chain has no issues.",
